  "prototype_changes": {
    "stretch": "Quantize each clamped counter probability to the nearest multiple of 1/65536 only for the logit input, then use a 65536-entry float logit table. Counter updates remain floating point. Includes the cost lookup and insertion-sort changes, with the original 8-byte counters.",
    "small": "The stretch prototype with the per-counter hash table capped at 20 bits instead of 22.",
    "format": "Both prototypes change probability predictions and require a versioned model before integration. They are not used by the retained implementation."
  },
  "retained_changes": [
    "Pack float probability and byte count together into five bytes, avoiding padding without splitting their cache accesses.",
    "Precompute diagnostic -log2 costs for all 16-bit arithmetic probabilities; model predictions do not change.",
    "Use stable insertion sort for the 9- and 19-entry predictor lists, avoiding temporary merge-buffer allocation.",
    "Pass a null numeric pointer for rows without numeric lanes instead of indexing at the end of the numeric vector."
  ],
